; bale-crier news timer — user-level. See bale-crier-news.service for the install notes.
;
; This timer, not the service, is the unit to enable:
;   systemctl --user enable --now bale-crier-news.timer
;
; The three times are literal on purpose: systemd expands no environment variable in a unit file, so
; a schedule setting would silently never fire. To change a time, edit the OnCalendar lines below
; and run `systemctl --user daemon-reload`.
;
; Seven minutes past the hour, not on it: the other project polls its news channel on the hour
; and every quarter, and this starts the digest after the :00 run instead of landing with it.
; The two-minute spread matches that project's own jitter, so the gap stays about seven minutes.
;
; The bale-crier.timer does not run the digest — it owns this timer — so the two timers cannot race
; over one seen set.

[Unit]
Description=Send the AI-news digest three times a day at 09:07, 15:07 and 21:07

[Timer]
OnCalendar=09:07
OnCalendar=15:07
OnCalendar=21:07
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=2m

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
